.VENV/
.env
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Generated datasets
data/raw/**/*.csv*
data/processed/**/*.parquet
data/processed/**/*.csv

# Exception: the extracted GFS point values are kept. The rule above exists
# because the observation sources are hundreds of megabytes and re-downloading
# them is quick; these are the opposite. Each run is about 28 KB on disk but
# costs roughly 0.76 GB of transfer and several minutes to rebuild, because a
# GFS file is 520 MB and only one grid point of it is wanted. Committing them
# means nobody on the team fetches the same bytes twice, and CI could use them.
!data/raw/noaa_gfs/
!data/raw/noaa_gfs/*.csv
